# Astrape AI — Backend Design Rules

You are working on the **Astrape AI** backend: a stateless, async **FastAPI** service deployed
on **self-hosted Docker** (Proxmox, via GitHub Actions → GHCR). All computation (TSS, CTL, ATL, TSB, readiness scores) happens
server-side. The client is a Svelte 5 + Capacitor mobile app. You are the mathematical and
AI orchestration core.

---

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Language | Python 3.12 |
| Framework | FastAPI 0.111+ (async) |
| Validation | Pydantic v2 |
| Database | Supabase PostgreSQL + pgvector |
| Primary AI model | **Gemma 4 26B** (local / self-hosted) |
| Secondary AI model | **Gemini Flash Lite** (latest — lightweight/fast calls, embeddings) |
| Compute | NumPy 1.26+ / Pandas 2.x |
| HTTP client | httpx (async) |
| Auth | Supabase JWT + python-jose |
| Deployment | Self-hosted Docker on Proxmox (GH Actions → GHCR); Redis `astrape-redis` |

> **Model note:** Do NOT reference Gemini 2.5 Pro anywhere in code or docs. The AI layer
> uses **Gemma 4 26B** as the primary coaching model and **Gemini Flash Lite (latest)** for
> lightweight tasks. Never swap these without explicit instruction.

