## Nested Interval Support

`IntervalPayload` supports deep nesting via `sub_intervals`:

```python
class IntervalPayload(BaseModel):
    name: str
    duration_minutes: int
    intensity: str              # "threshold", "Z4", "recovery", etc.
    watts: Optional[int] = None
    target_hr: Optional[int] = None
    sub_intervals: Optional[list["IntervalPayload"]] = None

IntervalPayload.model_rebuild()   # required for self-referential Pydantic v2
```

Stored in `training_plans.structure` JSONB. Example:
```json
{
  "intervals": [
    {
      "name": "Main Set", "duration_minutes": 36, "intensity": "threshold",
      "sub_intervals": [
        {"name": "Work", "duration_minutes": 6, "watts": 285},
        {"name": "Recovery", "duration_minutes": 3, "watts": 160}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

