## Database Schema (Key Tables)

**`athletes`** — id, user_id, display_name, ftp, max_hr, resting_hr, weight_kg, training_zones JSONB

**`workouts`** — id, athlete_id, source, sport, started_at, duration_seconds, distance_m, avg_hr, norm_power_w, avg_pace_sec_km, tss, hr_zone_{0-5}_pct, `stream_storage_path TEXT`

**`biometrics`** — id, athlete_id, date, hrv_rmssd, resting_hr, sleep_hours, sleep_score, recovery_score, body_temp_c, source

**`tss_history`** — id, athlete_id, date, tss, ctl, atl, tsb — `UNIQUE(athlete_id, date)`

**`training_plans`** — id, athlete_id, `planned_date` DATE, `duration_min` INT, `target_tss` NUMERIC, sport, `description TEXT` (Markdown notes), `structure JSONB` (nested intervals)

**`coach_memories`** — id, athlete_id, memory_type, content, context_ctl, context_tsb, context_date, `embedding vector(768)` — HNSW cosine index (`m=16, ef_construction=64`)

**`oauth_tokens`** — id, athlete_id, provider, access_token (encrypted via Vault), refresh_token (encrypted), expires_at

**RLS on every table:**
```sql
USING (athlete_id IN (SELECT id FROM athletes WHERE user_id = auth.uid()))
```

