## Common Patterns

| Pattern | Correct |
|---|---|
| DB access | `Depends(get_db)` — never a module-level client |
| Error handling | `HTTPException(status_code=..., detail=str)` only |
| Logging | `logging.getLogger(__name__)` — never `print()` in prod |
| Numeric rounding | `round(value, 2)` on all TSS/CTL/ATL/TSB outputs |
| Async | All I/O must be `async def`; sync SDK calls → `asyncio.to_thread` |
| AI output → DB | Always through `services/sanitizer.py` first |
| Strava streams | Supabase Storage blob — never relational rows |
| Secrets | `settings.*` only — never `os.environ` directly |

---

## Anti-Patterns — Never Do These

- ❌ `response_schema` / strict JSON output with tool-calling → use XML tags
- ❌ Calling Gemma/Gemini SDK synchronously in an async route → use `asyncio.to_thread`
- ❌ Writing AI-generated data to Supabase without `sanitizer.py`
- ❌ Polling Strava for new activities → use `activity.create` webhook
- ❌ Storing Strava stream data as relational rows → use Supabase Storage blobs
- ❌ Treating Whoop as source of truth for power/GPS → Strava/Garmin owns those fields
- ❌ Referencing Gemini 2.5 Pro → model is **Gemma 4 26B** + **Gemini Flash Lite**
- ❌ Computing TSS/CTL/ATL/TSB in the mobile client
- ❌ Skipping HMAC validation on any webhook endpoint
- ❌ Storing OAuth tokens in plaintext → use Supabase Vault encryption
- ❌ Cold-starting CTL from 0 → use the average-seeding strategy
- ❌ DB migrations to rename legacy columns → use Pydantic `Field(alias=...)` mapping
